{
  "$comment": "ADR-113 Amendment 4 fixture. JSON-RPC 2.0 POSTed to the daemon's OAuth listener with a bearer token, exactly as kb/query.* is. Clients branch on error.data.kind only; error.code is informative. Identifiers, hashes and times are examples; times are RFC 3339 UTC with milliseconds. Field names and kinds are normative.",
  "method": "kb/query.get, kb/query.list",
  "description": "D5's published view (built in PR-5): `view` is \"working\" (the default, unchanged) or \"published\". get returns the node's in-force revision exactly as a revision read does (kb/query.get with `revision`); list returns the nodes with an in-force revision, in node-id byte order, paged with `after`/`limit` like the working list, each with the working list's summary fields from that revision, its `version` and a revision summary, and the page carries `view`. An approved revision waiting for entry into force is not published; a node with none (never in force, or derogated) answers `node_not_in_kb` from get and is absent from list. With review off, and on an E2E KB, the published view IS the working view (same answer as without `view`). Any other `view` is invalid_params.",
  "transport": {
    "http": "POST /",
    "headers": {
      "Authorization": "Bearer <the person's IdP access token for this daemon's audience>",
      "Content-Type": "application/json"
    }
  },
  "examples": [
